          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "f6b359b0-6c8b-504c-92b8-3f1771f942cc"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{-7\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement II is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard"
    },
